00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.110
So, you can you can run a simulation

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:26.710
with a test bench that will test your

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:27.909
design

00:04:27.919 --> 00:04:29.950
and that will tell you if it's hopefully

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:31.150
Well, it will tell you if it's not

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.750
working correctly.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:34.310
Test benches don't guarantee that the

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:36.190
design is correct, but if you fail a

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.030
test bench, that does guarantee it's not

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.110
correct. So, run the test bench.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.110
And once you're satisfied that it passes

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.150
the test bench and it's working

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.870
correctly, you can then go to the chat

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:49.270
reviewer chat mode and just ask it to

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:52.310
